her speech saying  that the heroes can't put people at ease  because they are also afraid and this  shows that they are just like everyone  else  in the narration she wonders once again  who will save the heroes when they're in  pain and i'm calling it now this is  officially this is officially a chakra's  catchphrase because uh this is about the  third or fourth time she's uh thought it  or said it out loud but it's a valid  statement to make though because heroes  are human beings regular civilians might  not perceive them as that and so in that  way people don't really feel sympathetic  to heroes they don't really feel like  heroes are able to show weakness and  things like that which is why certain  people in particular are not really  caring about the fact that deku needs to  come back to ua but rather they just  think heroes are almost like these  robots that need to go out and protect  them anyway the spoilers say that we see  several panels showing different  characters including izawa who is still  in the hospital there's then another  flashback over chaco with her parents  and they are watching the fight of a  hero named eel boy but ochaku is too  busy looking at other people's  expressions eel boy wins and smiles at  her which makes achako laugh and for  those who don't know eel boy is the guy  from the war arc who was stabbed in the  back of the head by twice and yeah his  quirk was quite interesting i actually  mentioned it in a video i did about all  the different quirks in the war arc  basically what it does it lets him shoot  out these different eels from i guess  each of his hands and they seem to have  some degree of like uh sentience like  almost like dark shadow they kind of  operate on their own to an extent twice  not only start this guy in the back of  the head but toga then pretended to be  this person and then went on to stab  other heroes as well  in the present day ochako asks the  civilians to lend their strength so that  they can get through these difficult  times so that they can all smile  together again at this moment she  remembers toga crying and hesitates for  a second but then asks the civilians to  stay by deku's side while he rests just  quickly on that point about together  crying so this actually happened back in  the war arc and i think there's two  reasons why chaka hesitates here number  one is that she's a person who always  likes to see other people happy as we  know and the fact that she as a hero  made someone else cry instead of making  them smile i think that's what gave a  reason to pause for a second now the  second reason is possibly due to what  they actually spoke about in their  conversation as during that talk togo  was basically trying to explain that she  can't suppress her nature and that when  she loves someone she has to drink their  blood and transform into them that's  just the way she is and ochako wasn't  sympathetic to that she was just like  you know if you're gonna commit these  crimes you need to pay the price and  that is what caused toka to cry because  otaku didn't understand her  back at uwa uraraka says that deku has  tried to carry the burden of his quirk  all by himself but that deep down he's  just a high school student who has a lot  to learn and yeah this is something that  i think we often forget deku is  literally like what 16 years old i think  they're all like 16 or 15 years old so  you know all the stuff they're going  through that's pretty heavy to be  dealing with at that age and it's  reasonable for the adults to let him  into your way let him rest for a bit and  then go back out to the battlefield like  it's not that much to ask deku then  falls to his knees as he remembers the  first time he met uraraka at the ua  entrance exam and we get a double page  spread of her yelling at everyone saying  to let him stay here at this hero  academy at the same time we get a rare  narration from adult deku and he says  that this is the story of how he became  the greatest hero and also something  else there's something else will be  revealed in a few seconds but first the  principal remembers his speech about the  lack of understanding and intolerance  and how sometimes it only takes one step  for people to understand each other the  giant woman and kota then dash towards  deku and we see a mini flashback of kota  choosing his red sneakers with mandalay  those sneakers were obviously inspired  by coach's admiration for midoriya and  we kind of already knew that already  just based on his reaction in season 4  but still it's cool to get this 110  confirmation that you know deku is  kota's hero the narration from adult  deku then continues and he says that  this is also the story of how they all  became the greatest hero which is a  massive twist on that line that we heard  in like i think the second episode but  now i mean this is basically implying  that they are all collectively going to  be the greatest it's not uh it's not a  one person thing and i think this is  actually a good thing because if we look  back at all my time as the number one  hero as soon as he retired everything  went to crap basically but i guess in  the future if the whole of class 1a and  i guess other heroes as well if they are  all collectively the greatest hero i  guess that means that if one person  retires or if one person  dies then it's not the end of the world  because they all have each other's backs  if you know what i mean the chapter then  ends with present day deku on the ground  crying as kota and the giant woman reach  out to him and uh yeah that's the end of  it so uh one thing that wasn't mentioned  in this specific league was that the guy  from the very first episode you know the  guy with like the weird uh star-shaped  things on his head so that was the guy  that wished deku good luck on his  journey to become a hero and this guy  was in the crowd at ua with an umbrella  just watching the whole thing unfold so  i'm kind 